# NET-MESH-1 pass 1: the server roles split into processes (NET-ARCH §2M.2) - DesertServer --role coordinator |
# store | sim | gateway, linked over GNS mesh links that require a CA-signed certificate (a dev CA generated
# locally by `DesertServer --mesh-dev-ca <dir>`, never committed); the coordinator owns the authority map and the
# mesh step clock; clients connect to the gateway only, which routes each player's input to the sim the authority
# map names. `--role all` (the mesh of one) is unchanged.
# Runner: <scratch>/NET-MESH-1/run_mesh1.sh (base NET-1 run_net1e.sh + NET-2 run_net2.sh): 4 server processes,
# the editor is one client, the others are DesertNetProbe bots; console lines go to the sim's stdin.
# Дано: Editor + DesertServer + DesertNetProbe from task/NET-MESH-1; mesh = coordinator, store, sim 1, gateway as 4 processes.
# Когда: bot A walks 2000 cm along +X (--walk-cm 2000); the editor is B, standing at spawn 0.
